 Every new comment in an MA History thread becomes a `chris_comment` chunk, criteria inferred from text, linked by `source_ref` to the session. Approved by default — he wrote it deliberately.
 
+Implementation notes (session 6): `appendFeedback` — the one writer of the thread — calls `/api/ingest/comment` after the Sheet write, fire-and-forget; the endpoint re-reads the comment **from the Sheet** by timestamp (the thread is the record; nothing a client posts goes straight into the store). Comments over ~600 chars are split into single points on the blank lines he typed — verbatim, grouped never reworded, lead-ins ride forward and short tails ride back; tags are keyword tags, no model call. A comment is skipped if the store holds *any* chunk (live or superseded) with its timestamp, so bootstrap's whole-comment chunks and the hand-split 9/17 comment are never doubled. Scorecards in the thread (either shape) are not comments — §6.4 owns them. `npm run ingest:scores -- --comments` catches up anything the hook missed.
