+**Extract v4 (session 6), additive to the schema above:** `comparison_to_intended_outcome` is two comparisons — `vs_intent` (observed performance against the skier's own stated intent) and `vs_ideal` (intent and/or performance against what the task requires) — each `absent | partial | made` with `reference_quote`, `quote`, `prompted`. "Made" without the reference quoted is demoted in code (`comparisonFacts`, `/lib/extractStats.js`), which also still writes the v3 fields (`made`, `quote`, `intent_referenced_quote`) and adds `both_made`; a stored v3 object is lifted on read. `equipment.states_effect_on_observed_performance` separates an effect on what this skier did from a recommendation or its predicted benefit. `prescription.delivery_to_peer` is Mark's words only, and `speakerGuard` checks it against the session's speaker labels — the peer's restatement is moved back to `peer_restated` and logged in `extraction_guards`.
+
 Why a separate step: when the model reads and scores simultaneously it pattern-matches criteria as it reads and lands on "didn't check every box." Inventorying everything demonstrated *before* judging forces whole-picture evaluation. This enforces "evidence descriptors, not checklists" by structure rather than instruction.
 
