+| Exemplars are embedded on the extraction text, stored as per-line evidence + Chris's number, and carry no AI output | The query is `extractionToText(extraction)`; embedding the same thing compares like with like, and session 1 showed scores in embedded text compress every session into one band. An exemplar that showed AI numbers or rationale would teach the scorer its own bias back. Decided 2026-09-19. |
+| Exemplar slot is Chris's only; other mentors' scorecards are stored, not shown | He is the assessor; the levels the evaluator is taught are his. Gates/Mike cards are inter-rater data. |
+| The AI score a scorecard is compared with is pinned once (`ai_at_submit`, else at first ingest) | A rescore — including one made better *by that very scorecard* — must not rewrite history, or agreement drifts toward 100% by construction. |
+| Agreement headline and §1 targets count blind scorecards only | A card given after seeing the AI number is anchored; a card the scorer was calibrated on is not a test. Both are reported, neither counts. |
+| Knowledge ingestion is triggered by the app but reads from the Sheet | The Sheet row is the record. A client can ask for a session to be ingested; it cannot post a scorecard or a comment into the store that the thread doesn't hold. Failure never blocks the Sheet write; the CLI catches up. |
+| One complete instance alone = 3 at most; 4 = recurs, or (single-occurrence lines) complete and threaded | Two over-scores on 7uk7lnh came from "complete: 1 · partial: 0" having no rung. Applied with exemplars, tested on both scorecards, not tuned line by line. Decided 2026-09-19. |
